  "evidence": "Current full-course pavement independently digitized using provisional image controls refined by a dark low-chroma road-interior proposal and native-pixel review on the pinned native satellite raster, including the western return dogleg, upper straight chicane, northeast turn and complete eastern S. Operator describes a 2.3 km circuit; AMG publishes the full-course shape. Diagram coordinates, corner radii and stated lengths are not traced, scaled or fitted. Source way 191172211 version 4 is a venue fence, and the older OSM road chain does not match current pavement. Clockwise identity is separately described by the race promoter https://rpplind.com/circuits/. Alignment, travel direction and joins remain draft estimates; raster date and georeferencing error are unknown. The 112 provisional controls include a local-appearance proposal and explicit native-image corrections; fitted samples are not independent observations. The final trace uses 3 m arc sampling, a periodic 3 m Gaussian filter and 0.15 m simplification relative to that fitted curve, with source gaps no longer than 70 m. These processing tolerances are not positional accuracy. Raw controls on the western return were corrected before fitting. No official distance is fitted."
